        "bytes": 2028,
        "raw_sha256": "fe258f4f7d272a57a2fa1293a3b4663924b5a3e556f87f1ce03cd28a3837f959",
        "independently_decoded_literal": "\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}^{*}\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}=I-\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}^{2}\\,,\\hskip 20.00003pt\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}^{*}\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\perp}=-\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}^{*}\\,. (B.5)"
      },
      {
        "id": "A2.SS1.p3",
        "start_utf8_byte": 733596,
        "end_utf8_byte_exclusive": 742298,
        "bytes": 8702,
        "raw_sha256": "654bd2e3d43cfbb9332da21b4b76c2066f0c7aa4275c5a736d6bb2a6f1552873",
        "independently_decoded_literal": "We first apply this block notation to the reflection map \\mathsf{U} from ( 2.14 ). We use the same symbol for its pullback on observables: (\\mathsf{U}f)(x,y)\\coloneqq f(\\mathsf{U}(x,y))=f(x,2x-y)\\,. (B.4) This pullback is self-adjoint and unitary, and hence has block matrix \\mathsf{U}=\\begin{pmatrix}\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}&\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}^{*}\\\\ \\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}&\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\perp}\\end{pmatrix}\\,. Here \\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}=\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{U}\\mathsf{P} maps \\mathfrak{H}_{\\mathsf{P}} to itself, whereas \\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}=\\mathsf{P}^{\\perp}\\mathsf{U}\\mathsf{P} maps \\mathfrak{H}_{\\mathsf{P}} to \\mathfrak{H}_{\\perp} . Since \\mathsf{U} is self-adjoint and unitary, \\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}} is a self-adjoint contraction on \\mathfrak{H}_{\\mathsf{P}} . Writing \\mathsf{U}^{2}=I in blocks gives \\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}^{*}\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}=I-\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}^{2}\\,,\\hskip 20.00003pt\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}^{*}\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\perp}=-\\mathsf{U}_{\\mathsf{P}\\mathsf{P}}\\mathsf{U}_{\\perp\\mathsf{P}}^{*}\\,. (B.5)"
      }
    ],
    "mathematical_reason": "For the orthogonal projection P and selfadjoint involution U, A=PUP and B=(I-P)UP satisfy B*B=P U(I-P)UP=P U²P-(PUP)²=P-A² on the ambient joint Hilbert space. On ran(P), P is the identity, giving exactly B*B=I_macro-A². The two new ingredient edges and explicit nonselected printed-source AND route encode this derivation. They resolve the original missing ingredient without making B5 a required scalar-defect parent.",
